# Skill: feature-specifier

Read and follow `skills/feature-specifier/SKILL.md`. Use templates in `skills/feature-specifier/templates/` and fields in `skills/feature-specifier/schema.json`.

Announce: `Using skill: feature-specifier`.

## Phases (mandatory order)

1. Intake and ambiguity scan -- restate the request without adding features.
2. Clarification -- at most five questions in one batch; only blocking gaps; enumerated options preferred.
3. PRD synthesis -- In-Scope, Out-of-Scope, `FR-###`, `NFR-###`, data model, Gherkin.
4. Consistency check -- every FR maps to an AC; out-of-scope is not required behavior.

Unanswered questions become `ASM-###` with risk and owner. Do not implement code.

## Output

- `templates/prd.md`
- `templates/clarification-log.md`
- `templates/acceptance-criteria.md`

Gherkin uses observable `Given` / `When` / `Then`. Negative paths are required when authz or validation exists.

## Do not use

When a PRD is already approved and the user wants implementation, a trade-off, or only a threat model. Do not re-specify as a delay tactic. Do not ask questions already answered in the request or the repo.
